# process artifacts (audit/plan docs live in the working copy only)
#
# 2026-11-26, owner's instruction (gaps G-75): while every development step is local and nothing has
# been pushed, `/workspace/` stays **tracked**. Keeping the execution subset out of git made every
# KAT, board-profile and tier-parity conclusion "local_only": reproducible on this machine and
# invisible to anyone else, including a fresh clone. The receipts live next to the code now.
#
# 2026-11-26，按业主指示（gaps G-75）：在全部开发都在本地、尚未 push 的阶段，`/workspace/` **入库**。
# 把执行子集留在 git 之外，会让每一条 KAT / 板型 / 档位 parity 结论都变成 "local_only"：只在这台
# 机器上可复现，别人（包括新 clone）看不到。证据现在和代码放在一起。
#
# Restore the single `/workspace/` rule before the first push, or decide per subtree then. This is a
# temporary arrangement, and it is written down rather than remembered.
# /workspace/

# What stays out of git inside workspace/ is not "our work": it is vendored upstream trees and
# derived output. Ignoring these by name (rather than ignoring the whole directory) is what makes the
# line above safe -- 726 MB of third-party sources would otherwise enter the repository.
# workspace/ 里仍然不入库的不是"我们的工作"，而是随仓上游代码与派生产物；按名字忽略这些（而不是忽略
# 整个目录）正是上面那一条能安全注释掉的原因——否则 726 MB 第三方源码会进仓。
/workspace/referential_repos/
/workspace/qa/kat/build/
/workspace/qa/kat/generated/
/workspace/qa/qemu/build/

# Local Conan recipes are not ours to ship: they carry download URLs and sha256 pins, and the plan
# forbids moving them into the version library (PLAN line 416 and the hard prohibition on line 1004).
# Distribution goes through the private `hetai` remote; `conandata.yml` keeps only the requirement
# line and the version. Only the README is tracked, so the empty-looking directory explains itself.
# 本地 Conan 配方不该随仓发布：里面是下载地址与 sha256 钉子，而计划明令不许把它们搬进版本库（PLAN 416
# 行，以及 1004 行的硬禁止）。分发走私有 remote `hetai`，`conandata.yml` 只留需求行与版本。只放行
# README，好让这个看起来空的目录自己解释自己。
/workspace/conan/recipes/*
!/workspace/conan/recipes/README.md

# Process documents: kept locally, never shipped (owner's instruction, 2026-11-26 -- gaps G-76).
# The gap ledger and the plan carry self-criticism and internal sequencing, so the requirement is
# that they cannot be published **by any route**, not that we remember not to push them. Two locks:
# this list, and `procdocs_gate.py`, which fails the build when one of them reaches the index --
# including via `git add -f`, which bypasses this file completely.
#
# 过程文档：只在本地保留，永不随仓发布（业主指示，2026-11-26，gaps G-76）。差距台账与计划里有自我批评
# 与内部排序，所以要求是「任何途径都不能公开」，而不是「记得别 push」。两把锁：下面两条规则，以及
# `procdocs_gate.py`——它在本索引里发现它们就判红，包括绕过本文件的 `git add -f`。
/workspace/audit/
/workspace/PLAN-*.md

# agent-skill adapter views (generated symlinks/junctions; canonical source is .github/skills)
# Default: .agents only. Optional: .claude / .codex via `sync --harness claude|codex`.
# No trailing slash: a POSIX view is a symlink, which a "dir/" pattern does not match.
# Regenerate with: python .github/skills/_shared/skillkit/cli.py sync
# This template keeps views as links. A repository created from it commits a
# byte-identical .agents/skills copy instead (see .github/workflows/sync-template.yml).
/.agents/skills
/.claude/skills
/.codex/skills
/.github/skills/_shared/.skillkit/

# .vscode/: the shared files ARE committed (extensions.json / settings.json / tasks.json);
# machine-local editor state stays out
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/*.code-workspace
.vscode/ipch/

